Word Search Solver

This is a C-based Word Search Solver with a simple SDL2 GUI. It allows you to load images of word search puzzles, preprocess them, segment the grid, recognize letters, and solve the puzzle automatically.



Make sure you have SDL2, SDL2_image, and SDL2_ttf installed.
Build the project by running:

make

Run the GUI:

./gui



The GUI provides 5 main buttons, designed to be used from left to right:
Load Image – Select the puzzle image.
Preprocess – Cleans the image for easier processing.
Pre+Denoise – Cleans and removes noise (specks, artifacts). Use this if the image is noisy.
Segment – Detects and extracts individual cells.
Solve – Recognizes letters, reconstructs the puzzle, and highlights the solution.

You should choose either Preprocess or Pre+Denoise, not both.


All intermediate and final outputs are saved in the output directory in real time, so you can inspect each stage (loaded image, processed images, segmented cells, final solved puzzle).


gui.c – Main GUI program
preprocess.c – Image cleaning
layout_detect.c, cell_finder.c – Grid layout and cell extraction
predict_letters.c, emnist_mlp.c – Neural network letter recognition
solver.c, rebuild_puzzle.c – Solve and highlight the puzzle
